comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T11:44:24.626Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict 3040-item all-status/full-body read (no omissions), current init/gitignore/root-layout keyword searches and open/in-progress inventories, and full canonical pm-hous/pm-4uqm/pm-kynkl8 metadata plus relevant history establish prior fixes but no active owner for this reproduced defect. Preserve completed lineage and create only this bounded recurrence slice."
  "2026-10-21T11:45:36.545Z","harness:codex","Baseline reproduction on checkout c34a5327a: nested ensurePmGitignore removes outer Git ignore coverage. GitHub/security intake: no open PRs, Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning alerts all zero. All 24 open issues have existing PM-link comments except newly reported #1532, which this item owns. Batch dry-run safely refused a pre-existing non-regular tracker entry; the validated explicit two-item batch itself committed successfully, with no override."
  "2026-10-21T11:57:39.141Z","harness:codex","Regression sensitivity: before the production patch, the strengthened unit suite failed seven cases, including both nested-init orders and real Git literal/root-layout matching. After repair, 27 focused cases across the shared SDK unit suite, actual CLI nested-init journeys and existing merge-version-skew regression pass. Unrelated user text and CRLF content are retained, duplicate managed fences are consolidated, curated search/eval-queries.json remains trackable, and both merge-driver scopes are checked. Full source coverage is running. Batch preview refusal is expected fail-closed behavior under the completed pm-preview-path-refusal contract, not an ownership or permissions bypass."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T13:00:20.423Z","harness:codex","A repository-scoped ignore fence can serve several trackers. Reconcile only the active tracker rules, retain sibling scopes and user bytes, and verify exclusions with Git rather than generated text alone."
